      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there some specific doc format that these files are following? I figured we could make sweeping doc changes now if we wanted to when we are moving this interface.\n\nTypical existing AIDL formats:\n\n1) Enumerators are documented individually like the fields in parcelables and unions in this file. (no need to have `DEVICE_BOUND_KEY` twice).\n2) Function parameters are documented `@param \u003cname\u003e \u003cdescription\u003e` instead of `@\u003cname\u003e`\n3.a) Returns are documented with `@return`\n3.b) Either no language specific syntax, or use Java-like syntax for AIDL files. Don\u0027t use `Ok(\u003ctype\u003e)` (this is currently inconsistent in this interface).\n4) `@throws` is used to describe which ServiceSpecificExceptions or built-in exceptions are used for errors.\n5) function names aren\u0027t added to the doc comments. It\u0027s assumed the comment directly preceding a function is for that function. This change would reducing the odd tabbing in these doc comments.",
